{"headline":"The Minimalist Consumerist Pretender","roastReport":"You like to pretend you are an ascetically pure cinephile, but your algorithm reveals a consumerist addict wearing a linen shirt. Your feed is a hilarious mess of contradictions. You alternate between videos like I own 12 things: minimalism tour and actual total consumption slop like MASSIVE tech haul 2026, I bought every flagship phone, and MacBook Pro unboxing (again). You want the aesthetic of owning nothing while actively watching people buy everything.

Your taste in media is equally pretentious. You like 42 minute averages and four hour mammoth uploads like The entire history of cinema: a 4 hour video essay or Why slow cinema matters (90 minute essay). You created a playlist literally titled Video essays (never finish). You do not actually care about cinema or slow art. You just like having an unearned sense of intellectual superiority running in a background tab while you research your third keyboard build.

Your productivity obsession is purely decorative. You watch Desk setup that made me productive and Everyday carry update to optimize a life where you accomplish nothing. You have 47 videos rotting in Watch Later and a playlist named Tech hauls to research. You are not a minimalist. You are just an over-equipped spectator sitting in a custom chair watching other people unbox plastic.","brainrotScore":15,"brainrotTier":"Well Adjusted","redFlags":["Gave 3 likes to Gadget Goblin while watching I own 12 things: minimalism tour","Created a playlist called Video essays (never finish)","Liked MacBook Pro unboxing (again) while curating a capsule wardrobe","Keeps a list called Tech hauls to research like it is actual homework"],"personality":"Diagnosed with acute Aesthetic Dissociative Disorder. Patients exhibit an intense belief that watching videos about possessing fewer items negates the urge to buy every flagship phone. Severe symptoms include storing 47 unwatched longform videos as intellectual armor.","existentialQuestion":"How many four hour cinema essays do you need to pretend to watch before your desk setup actually makes you productive?","channelRoasts":[{"channel":"Empty Room","roast":"You watch a channel named after an empty room while mentally filling it with gear from your liked list."},{"channel":"Gadget Goblin","roast":"Three likes given to pure retail therapy fuel from someone who claims to love minimalism."},{"channel":"KurosawaLong","roast":"You use long form film analysis as background noise to feel superior to people who watch Shorts."},{"channel":"Frame by Frame","roast":"A single pity like for high art to balance out your endless addiction to camera gear hauls."},{"channel":"Keyboard Karen","roast":"You spent forty minutes watching someone click keys just to type the same unfinished thoughts in your notes app."}],"shareCardLine":"I watch 4 hour film essays to mask my obsession with buying flagship phones."}

